.TH VDR-SUITE.CONF 5 "Phase 60.15" "vdr-suite" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite.conf \- configuration file for vdr-suite
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdr-suite.conf
is the planned configuration file for vdr-suite.

It will describe database, HTTP listener and VDR backend settings used by the daemon.
Until the file format is finalized, selected runtime settings are available as environment variables.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_DATABASE_PATH
Overrides the SQLite database path.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_RECORDING_ARTWORK_ROOTS
Semicolon-separated mapping of backend IDs to absolute local Recording artwork roots.
Each entry uses the form
.IR backend=/absolute/path .
For example:
.PP
.nf
VDR_SUITE_RECORDING_ARTWORK_ROOTS=default=/var/cache/vdr/plugins/tvscraper;wohnhaus2=/srv/vdr-artwork
.fi
.PP
There is no universal default. TVScraper accepts
.BR -d / --dir
and otherwise derives its storage directory from the VDR cache directory, which is distribution and installation dependent.
The configured root must therefore match the actual local TVScraper directory for that backend.

Duplicate backend IDs, relative paths and malformed entries disable local artwork delivery for the parsed setting.
A backend without an explicit mapping cannot use another backend's root.

Recording artwork references received from a backend remain internal.
The daemon resolves them only below the root assigned to that backend and exposes opaque, authenticated
.B /recording-artwork/
URLs to clients.
Missing roots, unsupported file types, invalid image signatures, oversized files and paths escaping an allowed root are rejected.
.SH LOCATION
The planned system configuration path is:
.PP
.I /etc/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8),
.BR vdr-suite-dashboard (1)
.SH STATUS
This manual page documents the current environment boundary while the final configuration file format remains under development.
